sident, CEO & Director | Age 45 | Compensation: $3.9M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 225 people. Revenue per employee of $3.1M ranks in the top quartile among Financial Services peers, improving at 50%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $1.8M of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $90K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["NMI Holdings Inc is a mid-cap financial services business with a $2.9B market cap on $706M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +11% over the past three years and +29% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size. Operating margins are expanding by +27.8pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at 17% against a 8% cost of capital, a 9-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it.","The business throws off $413M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 58 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.08\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage of 19\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield of 3.6% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and within its sector the business captures 2.9\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $11.0M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 46% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Trading at a 67% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Valued at a 36% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"NMI Holdings (NMIH) Misses Estimates, Is It Still 22% Below Fair Value?","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/nmi-holdings-nmih-misses-estimates-011127449.html","date":"2026-11-07","ti