above the 2% gate)."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 10.5% over 3 years, 10.3% over 5 years and 29.4% over 10 years, and it has been lumpy (year-to-year swings of 84%).","Net reinvestment is nil (capex and working capital no more than cover depreciation), so fundamental growth is near zero.","Margins are expanding (+27.8% trend).","Capex runs only 0.6x depreciation (1.0% of sales), so the asset base is being harvested rather than grown.","Its Rule of 40 score is 66, clearing the bar for a healthy growth business.","Analysts expect 3.9% long-term annual earnings growth."],"own":["Insiders own a modest 1.6%, and institutions hold 99%.","Insiders have only sold over the past year (7 sales, net $11.0M sold).","It returns 3.6% a year to shareholders (3.6% in buybacks).","The share count has shrunk 2.6% a year over five years, steadily raising each holder's stake."],"people":["With about 225 employees, each generates about $3.1M of revenue, 6.3x the Financial Services median, and productivity has risen 49.7% a year.","That works out to $1.8M of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $3.9M (1x revenue per employee), and compensation governance scores well (2/10, lower is better).","Stock compensation averages $90K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"WATCH","conv":89,"head":"Watch: no strong case either way.","pros":["Trades 67% below fair value of $118","ROE 15.0% vs cost of equity 8.3%","Revenue grew 10.3%/yr over 5y","P/E 7.7x vs sector 12.2x","EV/EBITDA 6.7x vs sector 10.9x"],"cons":[],"flags":[],"need":["the model rates it HOLD"],"buy_below":100.47,"vc":{"base":118.2,"base_src":"dcf","bear":85.62,"bull":167.95,"alt_median":82.71,"n_alt":2,"gap":0.8488,"dispersion":0.1019,"level":"LOW","why":["DCF is 85% above the other models' median ($82.71)"]},"med":{"pe":12.155,"ev_ebitda":10.862,"pfcf":12.9041,"pb":1.3934,"roic":0.116,"gross_margin":0.4181,"fcf_margin":0.2507,"div_yield":0.0265}},"ticker":"NMIH","date":"2026-11-06"}